a por la exposición del esófago distal al ácido, lo que puede provocar molestias y complicaciones. Esta condición, también conocida como enfermedad por reflujo gastroesofágico (GERD), es un trastorno digestivo crónico en el que el ácido del estómago o la bilis irritan el revestimiento del esófago. El RGE es prevalente entre los pacientes con fibrosis quística, donde un porcentaje significativo experimenta síntomas relacionados. Además, se ha observado que el reflujo gastroesofágico puede empeorar o ser inducido por procedimientos de gastrostomía. En resumen, el REFLUJO GASTROESOFÁGICO es una condición que genera altos costes sanitarios y requiere atención médica adecuada para su manejo.\",12\r\n496,IBP,\"IBP, or Inhibitors of Proton Pump, is a class of medications utilized to treat acid-related conditions, particularly gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) and esophagitis. These medications are effective in alleviating symptoms associated with gastroesophageal reflux, making them a common choice for managing these conditions. In summary, IBP medications play a crucial role in the treatment of GERD and related disorders.\",4\r\n495,PH-METRÍA ESOFÁGICA,La pH-metría esofágica es una prueba diagnóstica que cuantifica el reflujo ácido y es la prueba de referencia para el diagnóstico de la enfermedad por reflujo gastroesofágico.,2\r\n502,ERGE,\"ERGE, or Enfermedad por Reflujo Gastroesofágico, also known as Esophageal Reflux Disease, is a medical condition characterized by the backflow of stomach contents into the esophagus. This condition leads to various symptoms, including heartburn and dysphagia, particularly in patients with a prolonged history of the disease. While manometry can be used to study ERGE, it is not typically employed to confirm the diagnosis of this condition.\",5\r\n90,EES,\"The upper esophageal sphincter (EES) is a crucial muscular structure that facilitates the opening during the swallowing process, allowing food to pass from the pharynx to the esophagus. It plays a significant role in the swallowing mechanism and can be impacted by various medical conditions, particularly in cases of dysphagia oropharyngeal. The EES is essential for proper swallowing function, and any dysfunction in this area can lead to swallowing disorders.\",11\r\n95,MANOMETRÍA,\"MANOMETRÍA is a functional diagnostic test utilized to evaluate the pressure and distensibility of the esophageal sphincter (EES) during the act of swallowing. This technique is particularly important for assessing esophageal motility disorders and swallowing function in patients experiencing oropharyngeal dysphagia. By measuring the pressure and patterns of muscle contractions in the esophagus, manometría provides critical insights into the underlying neural or muscular mechanisms, helping to differentiate between primary esophageal obstruction and mechanical obstruction. Often, this procedure is performed alongside impedance testing to enhance diagnostic accuracy.\",11\r\n92,DIVERTÍCULO DE ZENKER,\"The \"\"Divertículo de Zenker\"\" is a structural issue characterized by the formation of a pharyngeal pouch, which can lead to various swallowing symptoms that are influenced by the size of the diverticulum. This condition is associated with fibrosis of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES), which can affect its distensibility. As a result, individuals with Zenker's diverticulum may experience difficulties in swallowing, making it an important esophageal condition to recognize and address.\",2\r\n97,ASPIRACIÓN,\"Aspiration, referred to as \"\"ASPIRACIÓN,\"\" occurs when material enters the airway below the vocal cords, which poses a significant risk of respiratory complications. This condition is particularly associated with an abnormal opening of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES), where food can inadvertently enter the respiratory tract, increasing the likelihood of respiratory issues.\",2\r\n501,DIFICULTADES DE TRAGAR,,1\r\n500,ENFERMEDAD POR REFLUJO REFRACCTARIA,